186045443 true] [17592186561203 1072 #uuid "3a462c5e-dc46-5cbd-908d-8873a5836bec" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561203 1074 "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= x + 6 \\\\ -3x + 3y &= 18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = x + 6\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=x + 6\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x + 3y &= 18 \\\\\n-3x + 3\\left(x + 6\\right) &= 18 \\\\\n-3x + 3x + 18 &= 18 \\\\\n18 &= 18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always true. Therefore, we conclude that the system has infinitely many solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines intersect at infinitely many points (i.e., they coincide)." 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561204 1080 "intersect at one point" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561204 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561204 1083 #uuid "3d4a8325-79ab-5bbe-9c43-8395dff042e0" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561205 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561210 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561205 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561211 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561205 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561256 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561205 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561205 1077 "field-1" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561205 1078 #edb/ref 17592186561256 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561205 1079 #uuid "43673130-deba-5b98-8ce2-b4ee4ed0101a" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561206 1080 "do not intersect" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561206 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561206 1083 #uuid "4417ae70-0890-5813-a5ad-6509