\n$$\ny=-5x - 5\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-20x - 4y &=-8 \\\\\n-20x - 4\\left(-5x - 5\\right) &= -8 \\\\\n-20x + 20x + 20 &= -8 \\\\\n20 &= -8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)." 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561243 1080 "intersect at infinitely many points" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561243 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561243 1083 #uuid "a9537567-1850-5466-995f-5f2a3e4745df" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561244 1080 "do not intersect" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561244 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561244 1083 #uuid "aaa7f187-7fdf-5a83-ab02-69b55dfb828f" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561200 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561212 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561257 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561245 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561245 1077 "field-1" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561245 1078 #edb/ref 17592186561200 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561245 1079 #uuid "af3666b2-e413-595c-a093-783fa1dc8bf4" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561246 1080 "do not intersect" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561246 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561246 1083 #uuid "c60ae584-a9c5-5da2-b67b-9cea1d5ceb12" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561247 1068 #edb/ref 17592186561192 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561247 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561247 1071 "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: y = 4x + 2, l_{2}: -8x + 2y = 6$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561247 1072 #uuid "c74e2f77-c144-59ff-a39d-154078a44e94" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561247 1074 "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &= 4x + 2 \\\\ -8x + 2y &= 6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. The first equation already gives $y$ in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\ny = 4x + 2\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=4x + 2\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 2y &= 6 \\\\\n-8x + 2\\left(4x + 2\\right) &= 6 \\\\\n-8x + 8x + 4 &= 6 \\\\\n4 &= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)." 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561248 1068 #edb/ref 17592186561205 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561248 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561248 1071 "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: 5x + y =-1, l_{2}: -12x + 3y = 3$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561248 1072 #uuid "c7e53da6-3b28-54ab-be32-bc2afa7301df" 13194139536047 17592186045443 true] [17592186561248 1074 "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x + y &=-1 \\\\ -12x + 3y &= 3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x + y &=-1 \\\\\ny &= 